<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean oil tanker sinks, spills oil.</title>
<headline>S.Korean oil tanker sinks, spills oil.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>A South Korean oil tanker carrying 1,700 kilolitres of C-type fuel oil sank after hitting a reef late on Thursday, spilling oil off the southern coast of the Korean peninsula, maritime police said on Friday.</p>
<p>Police in South Korea's southern port of Tongyoung said they did not know how much oil had spilt.</p>
<p>&quot;It's leaking little by little,&quot; said one officer.</p>
<p>Seven vessels were spraying dispersant on the spill and setting up oil fences.</p>
</text>
